## Step 6 ladders read whole (974 lines) [done]
Provisional §5C (test, not evidence): money module L5 after calculations; MNY- {amount exact decimal, currency, when EDTF, stage, from{entity,fund,account}, to, purpose, buys[], authority[], source extent or table row, grade}; stages closed list budgeted, appropriated, committed, spent, received, transferred, owed, written off; never summed across stages; funds/accounts entities, accounts as aliases with scheme; rules = standards or duties; commitments = duties with money terms; ledgers stay tables in calculations, money fact may reference row; ~55 reqs L1-L3. Ladder rungs L0 cite, L1 money facts held (stage 1), L2 flows traced (stage 1), L3 rules and commitments (stage 2), L4 what bought/delivered (stage 3), L5 import/assisted/watched (stage 4). Needs M1-M13. Ladder §2 MONEY bullets. §10 "Every amount names its stage". Also EVENTS §5B: events module replaces chronology; kinds include payment, transfer, award, signing; relations authorises etc. PEOPLE §5A: people module, lines gave_to/received_from, owns_interest_in, officer_of, lobbies_for. Layer 5 order per ladder: entities, lines, people, local-facts, connections, standards, events, progressions, duties, bias, observation-log, query-language, retrieval, calculations, money.
Things to test: is "transferred" a stage or a flow kind? (In GASB, interfund transfer is a transaction type, not a budget stage.) "received"/"spent" mix budget stage with direction. Need separate axes: stage (budget phase / accounting basis) vs flow kind vs direction. Encumbrance=committed. Is money module after calculations OK? calculations is last; money uses calculations; but calculations' recipes over money facts? Check direction.
